summary: 'Static files come only from the pinned bundle that is hashed in memory (symlinks and special files refused, path normalisation). A directly opened SVG gets its own CSP, nosniff and CORP. The content type comes from the extension only, so a renamed .js can''t execute. Fonts are pinned and served from the same origin only. Lows: materializeGuiBundle should check the tree hash before writing (and use ''wx''); the kernel scan should ban script/foreignObject/href in SVGs. Info: align TEXT_EXT with the server''s type map, and skip dotfiles and symlinks in the build. All four folded into S2.'
